      "identifier": "CHEBI:86345",
      "proposal_count": 7,
      "status": "approve_scoped_substance_reference",
      "reasoning": "JCM414,378,438,537,862,866 and462 explicitly specify MgCl2·6H2O; JCM463 directs use of462 with other amendments and does not replace magnesium. Proposed notes retain the literal hexahydrate spelling and amounts. Both maintained candidate documents identify CHEBI:86345, magnesium dichloride hexahydrate, with CAS7791-18-6 and six-water chemistry. The readable component_name Magnesium chloride does not change the exact six-water component_id. No duplicate document is selected or merged."
    },
    {
      "identifier": "MICRO:0000178",
      "proposal_count": 1,
      "status": "approve_scoped_substance_reference",
      "reasoning": "TOGO M2491 explicitly states generic peptone5g. The component remains generic Peptone/MICRO:0000178 and does not add BD/Difco/Bacto product equivalence. Existing Bacto_Peptone and Peptone records sharing that CURIE are a catalog identity/ownership concern, retained for coordinator reconciliation; source specificity is not narrowed to a brand."
    },
    {
      "identifier": "CHEBI:29377",
      "proposal_count": 1,
      "status": "approve_scoped_substance_reference",
      "reasoning": "JCM1023/363 and their TOGO counterparts specify8%(w/v) Na2CO3 stock with2.5mL addition. The proposal keeps the whole stock under its own preparation identity and references Na2CO3/CHEBI:29377 only as a named constituent at8%w/v, with UNKNOWN completeness and no guessed solvent or receiving-medium normalization. Existing Sodium_Carbonate_Solution sharing the neat-salt CURIE is an explicit unreconciled catalog defect, not evidence that the stock is the constituent. This review chooses no owner document and does not resolve broader source hydration/supplied-form concerns."
    }
